                <h2>Why Conduct Compliance Audits</h2>
<p>In overseas advertising, account bans and ad rejections are the most frustrating issues for operations teams. A large-scale account suspension can interrupt the entire day's campaign plan, causing incalculable losses. Many teams only realize the importance of auditing after problems occur, but by then they've often missed the best opportunity for remediation.</p>
<p>Compliance auditing isn't "checking only when problems arise"—it should be a regular part of daily operations. We recommend each operations colleague complete at least one full audit per week, increasing to daily audits during high-risk periods such as platform policy adjustment phases.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Pre-Audit Preparation</h2>
<h3>Tools and Account Permissions</h3>
<ul>
<li>Ensure you have admin or operations role permissions on the advertising platform</li>
<li>Prepare the audit record form (use Feishu/Notion templates)</li>
<li>Access the account health dashboard (Meta Business Center/TikTok Ads Manager)</li>
</ul>
<h3>Confirming Audit Scope</h3>
<p>Which accounts and campaigns does this audit cover? Prioritize as follows:</p>
<ol>
<li>Primary accounts (top 3 by spend)</li>
<li>Newly launched campaigns (within 7 days of launch)</li>
<li>High-risk categories (finance, health, gaming, etc.)</li>
<li>Accounts with historical violation records</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Account Status Check</h2>
<h3>1.1 Access Account Health Dashboard</h3>
<p>Enter the advertising platform backend and locate the "Account Quality," "Account Status," or "Policy Compliance" section. Check for any warning notifications, restriction alerts, or pending issues.</p>
<h3>1.2 Verify Campaign Status</h3>
<ul>
<li>Confirm the account is actively running</li>
<li>Check for any campaigns paused due to depleted budgets</li>
<li>Verify account balance is sufficient to avoid automatic pauses</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.3 Reconcile Top-Up Records</h3>
<p>Review recent top-up transactions to confirm amounts received and arrival times match expectations. If you notice discrepancies or missing top-ups, contact your agency or platform support immediately.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Tip</strong>: Yoyu Media offers balance alert services—set thresholds and receive automatic notifications so you don't need to constantly monitor account balances.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Ad Creative Compliance Review</h2>
<h3>2.1 Visual Element Inspection</h3>
<p>Check against platform creative policies:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>People/figures</strong>: No bodily exposure, suggestive content, or images of minors</li>
<li><strong>Brand logos</strong>: No competitor logos visible, no unauthorized celebrity likenesses</li>
<li><strong>Text overlays</strong>: Character count within limits, no copyright-infringing fonts</li>
<li><strong>Animations</strong>: No rapid flashing, intense contrasting color blocks that may trigger violations</li>
</ul>
<h3>2.2 Platform-Specific Compliance</h3>
<p>Different platforms have varying requirements for creative dimensions, duration, and audio:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Platform</th>
<th>Common Issues</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Meta</td>
<td>Text occupying &gt;20% of image, "limited time offer" type incentive copy</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>TikTok</td>
<td>Brand logo in first 3 seconds, insufficient product footage</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Google</td>
<td>Exaggerated before/after comparisons, unverified medical claims</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>2.3 Violation Self-Check Checklist</h3>
<p>Copy the following checklist into your audit record and verify each item:</p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] No misleading before/after comparisons</li>
<li>[ ] No absolute language ("best," "#1," "100%")</li>
<li>[ ] No unverified efficacy claims</li>
<li>[ ] No violent or discriminatory content</li>
<li>[ ] No copyrighted music or video clips</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Copy and Landing Page Review</h2>
<h3>3.1 Keyword Filtering</h3>
<p>The following terms are high-risk on most platforms:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Efficacy promises</strong>: "Guaranteed to lose X kg," "effective in X days"</li>
<li><strong>Price incentives</strong>: "Lowest price," "lowest on the internet"</li>
<li><strong>Urgency tactics</strong>: "Only X left," "won't come back"</li>
</ul>
<p>If you must use these terms, consult platform policies in advance or moderate the language intensity.</p>
<h3>3.2 Landing Page Consistency Verification</h3>
<ul>
<li>Does the landing page content match ad promises?</li>
<li>Are there any dead links or slow-loading pages?</li>
<li>Are privacy policies and refund terms fully displayed?</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Handling Violations</h2>
<h3>4.1 Minor Violations</h3>
<p>If copy contains slightly inappropriate language or creatives have borderline issues:</p>
<ol>
<li>Pause the affected ad</li>
<li>Revise and resubmit for review</li>
<li>Document the violation reason to prevent similar issues</li>
</ol>
<h3>4.2 Serious Violations</h3>
<p>If you receive an official violation notice or account restrictions:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Screenshot and save the violation notice</strong> (critical!)</li>
<li>Submit an appeal within the specified timeframe (if the platform supports it)</li>
<li>Contact Yoyu Media support for platform appeal guidance</li>
<li>Check other active campaigns for similar issues</li>
</ol>
<h3>4.3 Account Suspension</h3>
<p>If your account is suspended:</p>
<ol>
<li>Confirm the suspension reason (check notification emails or backend alerts)</li>
<li>Prepare appeal materials: business license, advertising qualification proof, authorization documents, etc.</li>
<li>Submit appeal through official channels (avoid unofficial intermediaries to prevent secondary scams)</li>
<li>During the appeal period, maintain stable operations on other normal accounts</li>
</ol>
<hr />
