<hr />
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q: I found a creative has minor issues during audit, but the ad performance is excellent. Should I keep running it?</strong></p>
<p>A: Not recommended. Although not yet flagged by the system, platform reviews are somewhat random. If caught in manual review or reported by users, it may cause cascading impacts on the account. Prioritize revising or testing new creatives in a separate campaign.</p>
<p><strong>Q: My appeal was rejected. What should I do?</strong></p>
<p>A: You may appeal again, but provide more comprehensive supporting materials. If consecutive appeals fail, consider pausing that account and reallocating budget to other healthy accounts to avoid further triggering platform penalties.</p>
<p><strong>Q: The platform suddenly released new policies. Should I take down all historically performing creatives?</strong></p>
<p>A: Not necessarily. First assess whether historical creatives genuinely violate the new policy terms. If they're only "potentially risky" but not explicitly prohibited, you may continue running them with close monitoring. If the policy clearly bans them, complete the takedown before the deadline.</p>
